      "content": "The giraffe ('twiza') is one of the most beloved animals of Zimbabwe's national parks, from Hwange in the west to Gonarezhou in the southeast, easily recognized by its patchwork coat ('mavara mavara') and horn-like ossicones ('nyanga').",
